            <ArticleTitle>Hypertension in the Faith Community: A Four-Week, Nurse Led, Diet/Exercise Intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>225-231</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/CNJ.0000000000000420</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inadequate blood pressure (BP) control in hypertension carries a major financial and public health burden. This study examined the efficacy of behavioral and lifestyle changes on BP control among African American adults, aged 55 years and older in a faith-based setting. The study was supported by clergy who helped to engage participants in interventions. Nurse-led diet and exercise teaching with BP monitoring led to lower BP readings over a 4-week intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
